 "equipment_type": "Air-cooled screw chiller controller",
 "applies_to": "Daikin Applied Europe EWAD-TZD/MZD and EWAH-TZD/MZD air-cooled inverter screw chillers and the EWFD/EWFH free-cooling versions (MicroTech 4, software \"ETRA / OMEGA\").",
 "summary": "The EWAD/EWAH and EWFD/EWFH -T/MZD air-cooled chillers use a MicroTech 4 controller running the \"ETRA / OMEGA\" software. BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP comes from a POL908/POL904 module or the onboard software option. The list covers unit enable, mode and network setpoints, heat recovery, free cooling, variable primary flow, per-circuit refrigerant data for two circuits with one compressor each, energy monitoring, a shunt active filter and alarm objects.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 1,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Shares the core unit objects and instances (BV 2, MV 3, AV 3-7, BI 3/10, AV 900-905) with the other Daikin Applied Europe MicroTech 4 chiller guides (EWAT-B, EWA(F)T-B-C, EWWD-VZ).",
  "Heat recovery, free-cooling (EWFD/EWFH), variable-flow and shunt active filter objects only apply when the unit has those options.",
  "The guide prints many objects as AV_RED / MV_RED; they are listed here as AV / MV.",
  "BV 762 is printed for both C2'OFFMechPressHi and C1'Comp1'OFFVfdFault, and AV 1997 for both C2'FanStatus and C1'FanStatus; the second of each is listed without an instance.",
  "Units \"°Dc\" in the guide (temperature difference) are shown as dK. Alarm index/code ranges (0-65534) are shown without units.",
  "Revision 12/2023 is the first release of this guide for the ETRA / OMEGA software."
 ],
 "source": {
